{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed and verified. Three independent bugs stacked up, which is why the integration looked cursed.\n\n## Causes\n\n1. **Connect button 401'd for everyone** — it was a plain `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">`. A full-page navigation doesn't carry the SPA's `Authorization` header (that only travels on the fetch wrapper, since the sign-in token lives in `localStorage`), so `require_user()` rejected every click. That's the white `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}` page in ticket #214, and why Rivera only got through when support pasted the curl-built link by hand.\n2. **Authorize step 400 since the 2026-10-02 calendar deploy** — the scope string named `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR` twice (`:READ` + `:WRITE`). Intervals rejects a scope with the same area twice (`:WRITE` implies `:READ`), returning the unhelpful `{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}`. This killed even the hand-pasted workaround.\n3. **\"Reconnect after an hour\"** — Intervals' token response has no `refresh_token` and no `expires_in`; the token lives until revoked. The code assumed a 3600 s default TTL and its background refresher, finding no refresh token, flipped Rivera's healthy connection to `expired, reconnect` one hour in (log lines 37–40).\n\n## Fixes\n\n- `static/app.js` — Connect is now a button that POSTs `/api/intervals/auth/init` through the fetch wrapper, then `window.location.assign(authorize_url)`; the GET route was removed from `server.py` so the broken pattern can't recur.\n- `config.py:11` — scopes deduped to `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` (same effective access, each area once).\n- `server.py` — deleted the refresher thread, `DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL`, and `REFRESH_INTERVAL`; connections no longer expire. On the first 401 from the Intervals API the binding is cleared and the user gets a reconnect prompt (lazy revocation handling). `exchange_code` now sends only `client_id`, `client_secret`, `code`.\n\n## Verification\n\nRan the full flow against a local stub of the documented Intervals behavior (rejects duplicate scopes, rejects extra token-exchange fields, no refresh token, 401s revoked tokens): connect → callback → wellness round-trip all pass, tampered `state` is rejected, a revoked token returns 409 \"intervals access revoked, please reconnect\" and clears the binding, and reconnecting afterwards works. `node --check` passes on the edited JS. One note: a stale pre-fix dev server was squatting on port 8766 during testing — I killed it (PID 56792) so verification ran against the fixed code.\n\nCauses and the mapping to the colleague's note (§1–§4 applied; JWT-state, mismatch guard, and encrypt-at-rest deliberately not) are in `ANSWER.md`."}
